</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Chatbot System Prompts</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Figure </span><a href="#A2.F1" title="Figure B.1 ‣ Appendix B Chatbot System Prompts ‣ Invisible Saboteurs: Sycophantic LLMs Mislead Novices in Problem-Solving Tasks" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a><span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> depicts the schematic of the chatbot system that participants interacted with. Crucially, the task guidance context is only provided to the intermediate </span><span id="A2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Misconception Inference LLM</span><span id="A2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (Listing </span><a href="#LST1a" title="Listing B.1 ‣ Appendix B Chatbot System Prompts ‣ Invisible Saboteurs: Sycophantic LLMs Mislead Novices in Problem-Solving Tasks" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a><span id="A2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">), which is tasked to identify the student’s mental model and misconceptions. The </span><span id="A2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answering LLM</span><span id="A2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (which is either </span><span id="A2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;">High<span id="A2.p1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> </span>Sycophancy</span><span id="A2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, Listing </span><a href="#LST2a" title="Listing B.2 ‣ Appendix B Chatbot System Prompts ‣ Invisible Saboteurs: Sycophantic LLMs Mislead Novices in Problem-Solving Tasks" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a><span id="A2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, or </span><span id="A2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;">Low<span id="A2.p1.1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> </span>Sycophancy</span><span id="A2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, Listing </span><a href="#LST3a" title="Listing B.3 ‣ Appendix B Chatbot System Prompts ‣ Invisible Saboteurs: Sycophantic LLMs Mislead Novices in Problem-Solving Tasks" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a><span id="A2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) receives the user’s query and the misconceptions inferred, never the direct solutions of the task. We find that giving </span><span id="A2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">GPT-4.1</span><span id="A2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> an explicit list of misconceptions makes it </span><span id="A2.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">more</span><span id="A2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> corrective, which establishes the desired functionality of our </span><span id="A2.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;">Low<span id="A2.p1.1.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> </span>Sycophancy</span><span id="A2.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> condition without any additional prompting. This means that we require system prompting to then </span><span id="A2.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">undo</span><span id="A2.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> these effects to make the </span><span id="A2.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;">High<span id="A2.p1.1.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> </span>Sycophancy</span><span id="A2.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> condition appropriately more sycophantic. Lastly, we also show the evaluation results on the sentiments expressed by each condition in Figure </span><a href="#A3.F1" title="Figure C.1 ‣ Appendix C Additional Computational Evaluation Results ‣ Invisible Saboteurs: Sycophantic LLMs Mislead Novices in Problem-Solving Tasks" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a><span id="A2.p1.1.24" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.03667v1/img/LLM_api_calls.jpg" id="A2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:310/84;" width="310" height="84" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure B.1</span>. </span><span id="A2.F1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Diagram of the LLM API calls in conversation with the user.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="LST1a" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<div id="LST1a.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFF7DE;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx107" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx107.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0800;">Misconception Inference System Prompt</span><span id="lstnumberx107.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span>
