<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Computational Evaluation Results</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Figure </span><a href="#A3.F1" title="Figure C.1 ‣ Appendix C Additional Computational Evaluation Results ‣ Invisible Saboteurs: Sycophantic LLMs Mislead Novices in Problem-Solving Tasks" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a><span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> shows the proportion of the negative, positive, and neutral sentiments measured in each of the computational evaluation datasets for both chatbots. The only significant difference is the increase in negative sentiment for the </span><span id="A3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;">Low<span id="A3.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> </span>Sycophancy</span><span id="A3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> condition, when the user’s questions contain misconceptions.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03667v1/sentiments_v2.svg" id="A3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/167;" width="333" height="167"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure C.1</span>. </span><span id="A3.F1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sentiments predicted in the <span id="A3.F1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;">High<span id="A3.F1.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> </span>Sycophancy</span> and <span id="A3.F1.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;">Low<span id="A3.F1.10.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> </span>Sycophancy</span> LLM’s answers in the computational experiments on two query datasets — misconceived and open-ended questions related to the ML debugging tasks.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Knowledge Screening Quiz</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The </span><span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Knowledge Screening Quiz</span><span id="A4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> was administered to participants before the tasks, where the correct choice is indicated by the bolded statement. Each multiple-choice question is also accompanied by a slider from 0-100 indicating their confidence in the answer.</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What is the primary purpose of using k-fold cross-validation in model training?</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To increase the training dataset size</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To reduce the number of features</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To provide a more robust estimate of model performance</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To optimize hyperparameters</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Which of the following is a common symptom of overfitting in a basic machine learning model?</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">High bias</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">High variance</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Low variance</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Underfitting</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For a decision tree, which one of these structural assumptions is the one that most affects the trade-off between underfitting (i.e. a high bias model) and overfitting (i.e. a high variance model):</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The maximum depth of the tree</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The criterion used to measure the quality of a split (e.g., Gini impurity, entropy)</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The initial choice of features</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The use of pruning to remove branches</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Which of the following statements is true regarding precision and recall?</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1.i4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Precision measures the proportion of actual positives that are correctly identified, while recall measures the proportion of predicted positives that are correct.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Precision measures the proportion of predicted positives that are correct, while recall measures the proportion of actual positives that are correctly identified.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Precision measures the proportion of correctly identified positives out of all actual negatives, while recall measures the proportion of correctly identified negatives out of all actual positives.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Precision and recall are both measures of how well a model performs in identifying negative instances in a dataset</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Which of the following best describes the impact of a data distribution shift between the training and testing datasets in a machine learning model?</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1.i5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The model’s performance on the testing data is likely to improve because it has seen more diverse examples during training.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The model’s performance on the testing data is likely to deteriorate because it has not seen similar examples during training, leading to poor generalization.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The model’s performance will remain the same as long as the model’s hyperparameters are tuned correctly.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The model will automatically adapt to the new data distribution without any need for retraining or adjustments.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Participants’ performance on the Knowledge Screening Quiz is shown in Figure </span><a href="#A4.F2" title="Figure D.2 ‣ Appendix D Knowledge Screening Quiz ‣ Invisible Saboteurs: Sycophantic LLMs Mislead Novices in Problem-Solving Tasks" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a><span id="A4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The Brier score distributions are plotted, separated by the number of questions that participants got correct, where it is possible to get the same Brier score even with different numbers of correct answers, depending on the confidence rated. The overall range of Brier scores is 0.00-1.23 (</span><math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.69" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.69</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.69</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.32</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) and the number of correctly answered questions ranged from 1-5 (</span><math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=2.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=2.95</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=1.19" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.19</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=1.19</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">). The equation for the multi-class Brier score is given as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Brier Score}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\bigl(p_{i,k}-y_{i,k}\bigr)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Brier Score</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Brier Score}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\bigl(p_{i,k}-y_{i,k}\bigr)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Number of questions}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Number of questions</mtext></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Number of questions},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Number of multiple-choice answers per question}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Number of multiple-choice answers per question</mtext></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Number of multiple-choice answers per question},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{i,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Confidence that question $i$'s answer is $k$}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Confidence that question </mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">’s answer is </mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Confidence that question $i$'s answer is $k$},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{i,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{If question $i$'s answer is truly $k$},\\
0&amp;\text{Otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">If question </mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">’s answer is truly </mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Otherwise</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{If question $i$'s answer is truly $k$},\\
0&amp;\text{Otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03667v1/brier_dist.svg" id="A4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:262/210;" width="262" height="210"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure D.2</span>. </span><span id="A4.F2.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Distribution of Brier scores calculated from the accuracy and confidence calibration of participants in the <span id="A4.F2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Knowledge Screening Quiz</span>, where higher scores mean more miscalibration.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Mental Model Quiz</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The questions included in the Mental Model Quiz, where participants rate their confidence in the statement from -100 to 100. We use the same set of questions across the two tasks due to the nature of overlapping topics between tasks, which made sense to control the quiz as a source of variation. Note that some of the questions are slightly interpretive in nature. This encourages students to express varying magnitudes of confidence scores in response.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table E.1</span>. </span><span id="A5.T1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The<span id="A5.T1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> Mental Model Quiz</span>, which was administered in each task pre- and post-chatbot use.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A5.T1.9" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A5.T1.9.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"></td>
<th id="A5.T1.9.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mental Model Statements</span></th>
<th id="A5.T1.9.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">RF</span></th>
<th id="A5.T1.9.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">LR</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q1</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The balance of the dataset does not affect performance.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q2</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The difference in scale between features negatively affects performance.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q3</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Adding regularization improved the model’s test accuracy.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q4</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The data loading code contains a misstep.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q5</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The training dataset has outliers.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.6.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q6</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Leveraging feature importance analysis improves how to model weighs each feature.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.7.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.7.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q7</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.8.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The model does not suffer from overfitting.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.8.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.8.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.9.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q8</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.9.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The primary goal is to improve the test F1 score.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.9.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.9.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.10.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q9</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.10.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">random_state does not significantly affect model performance.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.10.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.10.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.11.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q10</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.11.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A primary problem is the lack of hyperparameter tuning.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.11.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.11.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.11.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.12.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q11</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.12.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A primary problem is that the dataset is unbalanced.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.12.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.12.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.12.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.9.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T1.9.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.13.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Q12</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.13.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A primary problem is that the features are not scaled.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.13.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">✗</span></td>
<td id="A5.T1.9.13.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.T1.9.13.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">✓</span></td></tr>
